# NOT ACTIVE ON THE CURRENT DEPLOYMENT. GitHub Pages ignores this file; it has
# no rewrite support at all, which is why the build prerenders a real HTML file
# per route and emits a 404.html fallback instead. Kept for Netlify.
#
# Note that on Netlify this rule is now a backstop rather than the mechanism:
# the prerendered files are matched first, so this only catches genuinely
# unknown paths. Left at status 200 deliberately — Netlify would otherwise need
# a separate 404 rule, and the app's own NotFound page sets noindex either way.
/*  /index.html  200
